and the Boston Globe reports a key  Greenland glacier is growing the glacier  had been retreating nearly two miles and  thinning 130 feet per year but a new  study by NASA found it started expanding  at about the same rate in the past two  years the researchers say that's because  of a temporary cooling off of the  surrounding ocean but they say that  means the progress will likely be  reversed when the waters start to warm  up again
 

